  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Hii Mission Technologies has $954M in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date, spread across 76 awards with an average award size of $12.5M. Obligations are down 17.8% year over year. Fiscal-year obligations moved from $596M in FY21 to $657M in FY22, $595M in FY23, $1.1B in FY24, and $1.2B in FY25, with FY26 at $954M so far. The General Services Administration is the largest buyer in FY2026 to date, obligating $759M, followed by the Department of Defense with $194M. Other buying agencies include the Department of the Interior with $443K, the Department of Education with $388K, and the Department of Homeland Security with $18.8K. Most dollars are in professional and technical services markets: All Other Professional, Scientific, and Technical Services accounts for $515M and Engineering Services accounts for $394M. Hii Mission Technologies also records activity in Other Aircraft Parts and Auxiliary Equipment Manufacturing at $29.7M and Other Support Activities for Air Transportation at $12.2M, and smaller reported markets include Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences at $5.3M, Electronic and Precision Equipment Repair and Maintenance at $1.8M, Educational Support Services at $1.5M, Custom Computer Programming Services at $881K, Software Publishers at $657K, and Ship Building and Repairing at $331K.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How concentrated are Hii Mission Technologies obligations by agency?",
        "body": "The General Services Administration is the dominant buyer, obligating $759M in FY2026 to date. The Department of Defense is the next-largest buyer with $194M. Other agencies account for much smaller shares, for example the Department of the Interior at $443K and the Department of Education at $388K. The Department of Homeland Security obligated $18.8K."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which markets receive the most Hii Mission Technologies federal dollars?",
        "body": "All Other Professional, Scientific, and Technical Services is the largest market with $515M in FY2026 to date. Engineering Services is the second-largest market with $394M. Aviation-related NAICS codes include Other Aircraft Parts and Auxiliary Equipment Manufacturing at $29.7M and Other Support Activities for Air Transportation at $12.2M. Other reported markets include R&D at $5.3M, repair and maintenance at $1.8M, educational support at $1.5M, custom programming at $881K, software publishing at $657K, and ship building and repairing at $331K."
      }
    ]
  },
